Patch summary:
Command buffers the guest flushes (vkQueueFlushCommandsGOOGLE) are recorded
on worker threads, two per guest process unless GFXSTREAM_PARALLEL_RECORD
says otherwise (0 records on the render thread as before). A process's
asynchronous submits and vkQueueSignalReleaseImageANDROIDAsyncGOOGLE run on
one thread of its own in the order they were decoded, each once the command
buffers it submits are recorded, so the render thread goes on decoding the
guest's next command buffer; one thread for all of a process's queues keeps
a submit that waits for a semaphore from blocking the driver ahead of the
submit that signals it. Recording took half of the render thread's time in
3DMark under WSL2. Vulkan commands that are not known to be independent of
pending work wait for all of their process's pending work first;
vkResetCommandPool waits for its pool's recordings. Each process has threads
of its own, as each render thread submitted on its own before: with one set
for every process, SurfaceFlinger composing a window over a game waited for
the game's whole backlog in each vkCreateBuffer, and 3DMark Steel Nomad Light
in a window showed about a frame a second while it rendered at 25.
vkQueueSubmit marks its fence waitable before it takes the fence's mutex
instead of while holding the global lock, since waitForFences takes the two
in the other order and a submit on the submit thread can now meet the
SyncThread waiting on its fence.
